var l = ["<script", ' type="application/ld+json">', "<\/script>"], c = ["<nav", ' style="', '"><a href="/"><img src="/logo_cmi.png" alt="Creative Metal Industries" width="140" height="71"></a><div style="', '"></div><a href="/blog" style="', '">\u2190 All Articles</a></nav>'], g = ["<div", ' style="', '"><a href="/" style="', '">Home</a><span style="', '">\u203A</span><a href="/blog" style="', '">Blog</a><span style="', '">\u203A</span><span>Duplex 2205 Steel Guide</span></div>'], h = ["<main", ' style="', '"><div style="', '"><span style="', '">Material Guide</span><span style="', '">June 2026 \xB7 9 min read</span><h1 style="', '">Duplex 2205 \u2014 Why This Super Steel Outperforms Standard Grades</h1><p style="', `">When austenitic grades like 304 and 316L aren't strong enough or corrosion-resistant enough, <strong>Duplex 2205</strong> steps in. With twice the yield strength and significantly better chloride stress corrosion cracking resistance, this dual-phase stainless steel has become the material of choice for offshore platforms, chemical tankers, and desalination plants worldwide. As an <strong>industrial metal supplier in India</strong> and <strong>SS pipe supplier in Vadodara</strong>, Creative Metal Industries stocks Duplex 2205 in pipes, plates, fittings, flanges, and bars.</p></div><h2 style="`, '">The Hybrid Structure \u2014 Austenite Meets Ferrite</h2><p style="', '">Unlike conventional austenitic stainless steels (304, 316L) which are 100% austenite, or ferritic grades (430) which are 100% ferrite, <strong>Duplex 2205 contains approximately 50% of each phase</strong>. This dual-phase microstructure is achieved through careful balancing of austenite-promoting elements (Ni, N, C) against ferrite-promoting elements (Cr, Mo, Si).</p><p style="', '">What does this hybrid structure give you?</p><ul style="', '"><li><strong>From the ferrite phase:</strong> High strength (yield ~450 MPa vs 170 MPa for 316L), resistance to chloride stress corrosion cracking (SCC), magnetic response</li><li><strong>From the austenite phase:</strong> Good toughness and ductility, weldability, corrosion resistance in reducing acids</li><li><strong>Synergy:</strong> The grain boundary between the two phases acts as a barrier to crack propagation \u2014 neither phase can fail independently</li></ul><h2 style="', '">Chemical Composition \u2014 Duplex 2205</h2><div style="', '"><table style="', '"><thead><tr style="', '"><th style="', '">Element</th><th style="', '">UNS S31803</th><th style="', '">UNS S32205</th><th style="', '">Role</th></tr></thead><tbody>', '</tbody></table></div><p style="', '">PREN = %Cr + 3.3\xD7%Mo + 16\xD7%N = 22 + 3.3\xD73.1 + 16\xD70.17 \u2248 <strong>35</strong>. This comfortably exceeds the PREN 32 threshold for resistance to most industrial chloride environments.</p><h2 style="', '">Mechanical Properties \u2014 2\xD7 Stronger Than 316L</h2><div style="', '"><table style="', '"><thead><tr style="', '"><th style="', '">Property</th><th style="', '">Duplex 2205</th><th style="', '">SS 316L (for comparison)</th></tr></thead><tbody>', '</tbody></table></div><p style="', '">The 2.5\xD7 higher yield strength means Duplex 2205 piping and vessels can be designed with thinner walls, reducing weight by 30-40% compared to 316L designs for the same pressure rating. This is a significant cost and weight advantage in offshore and marine structures.</p><h2 style="', '">Key Applications of Duplex 2205</h2><div style="', '">', '</div><h2 style="', '">Corrosion Resistance \u2014 Chloride SCC Immunity</h2><p style="', '">The single most important advantage of Duplex 2205 over austenitic grades is its <strong>resistance to Chloride Stress Corrosion Cracking (SCC)</strong>. Austenitic grades like 304 and 316L are susceptible to sudden brittle fracture under the combination of tensile stress + chloride ions + temperature above 60\xB0C. This failure mode gives no warning and is catastrophic.</p><p style="', '">The ferrite phase in Duplex 2205 is inherently immune to chloride SCC. Since cracks cannot propagate through the ferrite grains, the duplex structure effectively stops SCC crack growth. This makes Duplex 2205 the go-to material for hot chloride environments where 316L would fail suddenly and without warning.</p><h2 style="', '">Weldability Considerations</h2><p style="', '">Duplex 2205 is weldable by TIG, MIG, MMA, and SAW \u2014 but requires more care than austenitic grades to maintain the critical 30-70% ferrite balance in the weld zone:</p><ul style="', '"><li><strong>Filler metal:</strong> ER2209 / E2209 \u2014 over-alloyed with nickel (~9%) to promote austenite in the weld metal</li><li><strong>Heat input:</strong> 0.5\u20132.5 kJ/mm. Too low = excess ferrite (brittle, poor corrosion). Too high = sigma phase precipitation</li><li><strong>Interpass temperature:</strong> Maximum 150\xB0C \u2014 do not overheat</li><li><strong>No preheat:</strong> Never preheat duplex (promotes sigma phase above 300\xB0C)</li><li><strong>Back purge:</strong> Mandatory argon + 2-3% nitrogen back purge to promote austenite on root side</li><li><strong>PWHT:</strong> Generally NOT required. If phase balance is disrupted, full solution anneal (1020-1100\xB0C + water quench) is the only fix</li><li><strong>Ferrite check:</strong> Verify 30-70% ferrite in production welds using ferritoscope or metallographic examination</li></ul><h2 style="', '">Why Source Duplex 2205 from Creative Metal Industries?</h2><ul style="', '"><li><strong>Ready stock:</strong> Duplex 2205 seamless pipes (ASTM A790), plates (A240), fittings (A815), flanges (A182 F51) at our Vadodara warehouse</li><li><strong>Premium mills:</strong> Sandvik (Sweden), Outokumpu (Finland), Tubacex (Spain), Ratnamani (India)</li><li><strong>Full testing:</strong> MTC 3.1/3.2 with ferrite count, impact test at -46\xB0C, ASTM A923 (intermetallic phase detection)</li><li><strong>Corrosion test certificates:</strong> ASTM G48 Method A (pitting test) at specified temperature available</li><li><strong>Specialist knowledge:</strong> 15+ years supplying duplex to offshore, desalination, and chemical EPC contractors across India</li><li><strong>Export ready:</strong> Dubai, Abu Dhabi, Oman, Saudi Arabia, Kuwait \u2014 complete documentation for Middle East projects</li></ul><h2 style="', '">Frequently Asked Questions \u2014 Duplex 2205</h2><div style="', '">', '</div><div style="', '"><h2 style="', '">Need Duplex 2205 Pipes, Plates or Fittings?</h2><p style="', '">Ready stock \u2014 Sandvik, Outokumpu, Tubacex. MTC with ferrite count + impact test. Same-day dispatch from Vadodara.</p><div style="', '"><a href="tel:+919998280619" style="', '">\u{1F4DE} +91 99982 80619</a><a href="https://wa.me/919998280619" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="', '">\u{1F4AC} WhatsApp</a><a href="/#contact" style="', '">Send Enquiry \u2192</a></div></div><h3 style="', '">Related Articles & Products</h3><div style="', '">', "</div></main>"], u = ["<footer", ' style="', '"><p><strong style="', '">Creative Metal Industries</strong> \u2014 Duplex 2205 Supplier India | Industrial Metal Supplier Vadodara</p><p><a href="tel:+919998280619" style="', '">+91 99982 80619</a> | <a href="https://www.creativemetalind.com" style="', '">creativemetalind.com</a></p></footer>'], f = ["<tr", ' style="', '"><td style="', '">', '</td><td style="', '">', '</td><td style="', '">', '</td><td style="', '">', "</td></tr>"], b = ["<tr", ' style="', '"><td style="', '">', '</td><td style="', '">', '</td><td style="', '">', "</td></tr>"], y = ["<div", ' style="', '"><span style="', '">', '</span><h3 style="', '">', '</h3><p style="', '">', "</p></div>"], x = ["<details", ' style="', '"><summary style="', '">', '</summary><p style="', '">', "</p></details>"], w = ["<a", ' style="', '"><!--$-->', "<!--/--> \u2192</a>"];
const v = JSON.stringify({ "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: "Duplex 2205 \u2014 Why This Super Steel Outperforms Standard Grades", author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Creative Metal Industries" }, publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Creative Metal Industries", logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: "https://www.creativemetalind.com/logo_cmi.png" } }, datePublished: "2026-06-17", image: "https://www.creativemetalind.com/img/duplex-steel.webp", url: "https://www.creativemetalind.com/blog/duplex-2205-steel-guide" }), C = JSON.stringify({ "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", mainEntity: [{ "@type": "Question", name: "What is Duplex 2205 stainless steel?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Duplex 2205 (UNS S31803/S32205) is a dual-phase stainless steel containing approximately 50% austenite and 50% ferrite. This hybrid microstructure gives it roughly twice the yield strength of 316L (450 MPa vs 170 MPa) while maintaining excellent corrosion resistance with a PREN of ~35. It contains 22% Cr, 5.5% Ni, 3% Mo, and 0.15% N." } }, { "@type": "Question", name: "Where is Duplex 2205 used?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Duplex 2205 is used in: chemical tankers (cargo tanks), desalination plants (high-pressure RO piping), offshore oil & gas platforms, heat exchangers in chloride service, FGD (flue gas desulphurisation) scrubbers, bridges and structural components in coastal environments, pulp & paper digesters, and anywhere that requires high strength + chloride corrosion resistance." } }, { "@type": "Question", name: "Can Duplex 2205 be welded?", acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: "Yes, but with strict heat input control. Welding must maintain 30-70% ferrite in the weld metal and HAZ. Use matching filler (ER2209/E2209) with slightly higher nickel to promote austenite formation. Heat input range: 0.5-2.5 kJ/mm. Interpass temperature max 150\xB0C. Solution anneal at 1020-1100\xB0C followed by water quench if phase balance is disrupted." } }] });
